 6. Orchestration-Based Saga (In Depth)

 Flow Example


Saga Orchestrator
   |
   | CreateOrder
   ↓
Order Service
   |
   | OrderCreated
   ↓
Payment Service
   |
   | PaymentSuccess
   ↓
Inventory Service
   |
   | InventorySuccess
   ↓
Saga → COMPLETED


 Failure


InventoryFailed
   ↓
Saga Orchestrator
   ↓
RefundPayment
   ↓
CancelOrder


---

 Orchestrator Example (Spring Boot style)

java
public class OrderSaga {

  public void startSaga() {
    send(new CreateOrderCmd());
  }

  public void onPaymentFailed() {
    send(new CancelOrderCmd());
  }

  public void onInventoryFailed() {
    send(new RefundPaymentCmd());
    send(new CancelOrderCmd());
  }
}


 Characteristics

✅ Clear flow  
✅ Easy monitoring  
✅ Centralized logic  
❌ Single point of control  
❌ Slightly tighter coupling

